---
description: Trigger patch - a content edit to any .md misses the doc skills' keyword triggers, so this glob routes it.
globs: "**/*.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

Authoring or restructuring any `.md` (README, ADR, runbook) - load the `markdown-style` skill under
`.cursor/skills/` first; skip the load when it is already in context. Its own keywords only catch an
explicit lint ask, so a plain content edit misses it - which is exactly the blind spot this glob
patches.

ADR / Mermaid-diagram / C4 work also loads `docs-as-code` (same blind spot: its triggers are the
doc-type keywords, not an edit).

If neither skill is loaded, hold the line on the highest-value rules: one H1, sentence-case headings,
fenced code with a language, and tables over prose for anything enumerable.

This is guidance, auto-attached by glob (not a hard block). Skip one-line tweaks.
